1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,978
OK.

2
00:00:02,978 --> 00:00:06,571
If you want to adopt an animal,

3
00:00:06,571 --> 00:00:08,934
first we need to know some references.

4
00:00:08,934 --> 00:00:10,164
References?

5
00:00:10,164 --> 00:00:11,912
People we know?

6
00:00:11,912 --> 00:00:14,890
Friends, teachers....

7
00:00:14,890 --> 00:00:17,868
We need to talk to some people about you.

8
00:00:17,868 --> 00:00:19,841
We want to be sure that you're responsible

9
00:00:19,841 --> 00:00:23,046
and that you can take good care of an animal.

10
00:00:23,046 --> 00:00:25,110
Then you have to fill out this form

11
00:00:25,110 --> 00:00:26,802
about your family background.

12
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:28,302
Is that it?

13
00:00:28,302 --> 00:00:30,220
No, there's more.

14
00:00:30,220 --> 00:00:33,910
We need to know about your history with animals.

15
00:00:33,910 --> 00:00:35,736
Have you ever owned an animal?

16
00:00:35,736 --> 00:00:36,060
Yes.

17
00:00:36,060 --> 00:00:43,692
We had a cat when I was eight years old.

18
00:00:43,692 --> 00:00:45,919
I love cats.

19
00:00:45,919 --> 00:00:48,319
Do you have any animals now?

20
00:00:48,319 --> 00:00:48,767
Unfortunately, no.

21
00:00:48,767 --> 00:00:49,215
Anything else?

22
00:00:49,215 --> 00:00:51,217
We also like to know

23
00:00:51,217 --> 00:00:52,993
your reasons for wanting an animal.

24
00:00:52,993 --> 00:00:57,066
Just to hold it and cuddle with it.

25
00:00:57,066 --> 00:01:00,416
Just to have as a pet.

26
00:01:00,416 --> 00:01:01,702
I love animals.

27
00:01:01,702 --> 00:01:05,515
To have a friend -- a pal.

28
00:01:05,515 --> 00:01:08,493
You know, man's best friend is his dog.

29
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:10,413
And one thing more.

30
00:01:10,413 --> 00:01:12,328
If you're under twenty-one years of age ...

31
00:01:12,328 --> 00:01:13,185
That's me.

32
00:01:13,185 --> 00:01:15,596
Then an adult must sign for you.

33
00:01:15,596 --> 00:01:16,169
Uh-oh.

34
00:01:16,169 --> 00:01:16,649
No problem.

35
00:01:16,649 --> 00:01:18,716
My parents will think it's a good idea.

36
00:01:18,716 --> 00:01:20,816
I'll be back with them.

37
00:01:20,816 --> 00:01:25,243
If the real owners don't come to claim Gemma ...

38
00:01:25,243 --> 00:01:27,411
After forty-eight hours.

39
00:01:27,411 --> 00:01:28,811
But please call first.

40
00:01:28,811 --> 00:01:31,779
Thanks for your information and for being so helpful.

41
00:01:31,779 --> 00:01:32,681
It's my pleasure.

42
00:01:32,681 --> 00:01:33,772
Nice talking to both of you.

43
00:01:33,772 --> 00:01:34,135
Thanks again.

44
00:01:34,135 --> 00:01:34,335
Bye.

45
00:01:34,317 --> 00:01:37,095
Maybe the real owners will come to claim her.

46
00:01:37,095 --> 00:01:38,611
Her eyes look so sad.

47
00:01:38,611 --> 00:01:40,300
She must really miss them.

48
00:01:40,300 --> 00:01:43,691
I see you're both animal lovers.

49
00:01:43,691 --> 00:01:45,318
We are.

50
00:01:45,318 --> 00:01:45,518
Good-bye, Miss Aborn.

51
00:01:45,318 --> 00:01:46,411
We'll call in a couple of days.

52
00:01:46,411 --> 00:01:49,207
Good-bye, and thanks for bringing Gemma in.

53
00:01:49,207 --> 00:01:59,118
Bye.

54
00:01:59,118 --> 00:02:02,873
I keep thinking about the dog -- about Gemma,

55
00:02:02,873 --> 00:02:05,074
alone in the animal shelter.

56
00:02:05,074 --> 00:02:06,074
I know.

57
00:02:06,074 --> 00:02:08,479
But I promise you, Alexandra,

58
00:02:08,479 --> 00:02:10,612
the dog is just fine.

59
00:02:10,612 --> 00:02:12,830
They're very kind to the animals.

60
00:02:12,830 --> 00:02:13,670
I know they are.

61
00:02:13,670 --> 00:02:15,699
I mean about her being alone.

62
00:02:15,699 --> 00:02:18,154
Even if they are kind to Gemma,

63
00:02:18,154 --> 00:02:19,964
she's still alone, without her family.

64
00:02:19,964 --> 00:02:21,617
Ready, folks?

65
00:02:21,617 --> 00:02:22,942
Are you ready, Alexandra?

66
00:02:22,942 --> 00:02:24,942
Yes, I'm ready.

67
00:02:24,942 --> 00:02:27,540
I'll have the chef's salad, please.

68
00:02:27,540 --> 00:02:30,184
I will have a cheeseburger, medium rare,

69
00:02:30,184 --> 00:02:33,376
with raw onion, and french fries, please.

70
00:02:33,376 --> 00:02:36,326
Anything to drink?

71
00:02:36,326 --> 00:02:38,032
A diet cola, please.

72
00:02:38,032 --> 00:02:40,032
Ginger ale with lots of ice for me, thank you.

73
00:02:40,032 --> 00:02:40,810
I've got it.

74
00:02:40,810 --> 00:02:41,550
Thanks.

75
00:02:41,550 --> 00:02:43,788
Aren't you surprised

76
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:46,152
that the animal shelter is so careful

77
00:02:46,152 --> 00:02:48,046
about finding homes for the animals?

78
00:02:48,046 --> 00:02:49,744
No, I'm not.

79
00:02:49,744 --> 00:02:51,569
And a cheeseburger, medium rare,

80
00:02:51,569 --> 00:02:53,298
with onion and french fries.

81
00:02:53,298 --> 00:02:56,940
And a ginger ale with lots of ice.

82
00:02:56,940 --> 00:02:58,678
Salad dressing?

83
00:02:58,678 --> 00:03:02,168
Hey, I wanted you to hear my new sound system

84
00:03:02,168 --> 00:03:04,634
when the dog scratched on the front door.

85
00:03:04,634 --> 00:03:05,452
Let's finish eating,

86
00:03:05,452 --> 00:03:07,612
and then we'll go back to my house.

87
00:03:07,612 --> 00:03:11,190
I want you to hear my new tapes.

88
00:03:11,190 --> 00:03:31,435
I've got some great new dance music.

89
00:03:31,435 --> 00:03:31,935
Hello.

90
00:03:31,935 --> 00:03:32,935
Stewart residence.

91
00:03:32,935 --> 00:03:33,435
Hello.

92
00:03:33,435 --> 00:03:35,435
Is Robbie Stewart there?

93
00:03:35,435 --> 00:03:35,635
This is he.

94
00:03:35,435 --> 00:03:35,933
Who's this?

95
00:03:35,933 --> 00:03:38,378
This is Linda Aborn from the animal shelter.

96
00:03:38,378 --> 00:03:40,369
It's Linda from the animal shelter.

97
00:03:40,369 --> 00:03:41,036
Yes, Linda.

98
00:03:41,036 --> 00:03:41,369
Hi.

99
00:03:41,369 --> 00:03:46,700
We have good news and bad news, Robbie.

100
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:47,075
Oh?

101
00:03:47,075 --> 00:03:50,394
The good news is that the Levinsons have come by

102
00:03:50,394 --> 00:03:51,758
to pick up the dog.

103
00:03:51,758 --> 00:03:54,781
The bad news is, you won't be able to adopt the dog.

104
00:03:54,781 --> 00:03:55,259
That's OK.

105
00:03:55,259 --> 00:04:00,770
Come by one day and look at some of the other dogs.

106
00:04:00,770 --> 00:04:02,695
I'm sure there's one for you.

107
00:04:02,695 --> 00:04:03,435
Thanks, Robbie.

108
00:04:03,435 --> 00:04:07,171
And the Levinsons thank you for bringing their dog to us.

109
00:04:07,171 --> 00:04:08,504
Thanks, Linda.

110
00:04:08,504 --> 00:04:16,105
Bye.

111
00:04:16,105 --> 00:04:19,083
The owners claimed Gemma?

112
00:04:19,083 --> 00:04:20,546
That's right.

113
00:04:20,546 --> 00:04:22,060
I'm glad for the dog.

114
00:04:22,060 --> 00:04:25,038
I guess I am, too.

115
00:04:25,038 --> 00:04:26,674
She said if I come by,

116
00:04:26,674 --> 00:04:30,994
she'll help me find another dog.

117
00:04:30,994 --> 00:04:33,994
Come on. Let's dance.
